"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,711\nThe Learning Brain. Series 6: Neuromyths\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,416\nEpisode 11\n\n3\n00:00:07,496 --> 00:00:10,864\nDigital natives and multitaskers\n\n4\n00:00:13,664 --> 00:00:16,138\nToday's students grew up with screens.\n\n5\n00:00:16,406 --> 00:00:18,672\nSo they must be fluent with information,\n\n6\n00:00:18,857 --> 00:00:21,429\nand able to handle several streams at once.\n\n7\n00:00:21,816 --> 00:00:24,100\nThat is the digital native idea.\n\n8\n00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:28,211\nThe term came from a 2001 article by Marc Prensky.\n\n9\n00:00:28,723 --> 00:00:33,702\nHe argued that students born into digital technology think and learn differently,\n\n10\n00:00:33,986 --> 00:00:36,323\nand that teaching must change to match.\n\n11\n00:00:36,493 --> 00:00:41,824\nIn 2017, Paul Kirschner and Pedro De Bruyckere reviewed the evidence.\n\n12\n00:00:42,268 --> 00:00:45,908\nThey found no sign of an information savvy generation.\n\n13\n00:00:46,444 --> 00:00:50,380\nUsing technology often is not the same as using it well,\n\n14\n00:00:50,638 --> 00:00:53,793\nfor searching, judging sources or learning.\n\n15\n00:00:53,963 --> 00:00:56,057\nThe second claim, multitasking,\n\n16\n00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:57,278\nfares no better.\n\n17\n00:00:57,692 --> 00:01:00,870\nPeople do not really do two thinking tasks at once.\n\n18\n00:01:01,202 --> 00:01:02,505\nThey switch between them.\n\n19\n00:01:02,996 --> 00:01:05,879\nEach switch has a cost in time and errors,\n\n20\n00:01:06,074 --> 00:01:10,234\nand designing learning around multitasking hinders rather than helps.\n\n21\n00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:12,101\nThe myth can hurt students.\n\n22\n00:01:12,425 --> 00:01:15,241\nIf we assume they already have digital skills,\n\n23\n00:01:15,394 --> 00:01:16,614\nwe may not teach them.\n\n24\n00:01:16,971 --> 00:01:20,768\nAnd older instructors may wrongly assume they cannot keep up.\n\n25\n00:01:20,938 --> 00:01:26,977\nThe grain of truth: young people are often comfortable with devices and quick to try new apps.\n\n26\n00:01:27,277 --> 00:01:29,620\nBut comfort is not the same as skill.\n\n27\n00:01:29,790 --> 00:01:31,963\nOur next series looks at digital learning: screens,\n\n28\n00:01:32,321 --> 00:01:35,905\nslides, video and online courses,\n\n29\n00:01:36,169 --> 00:01:38,334\nand what the evidence says about each.\n\n30\n00:01:38,504 --> 00:01:39,664\nDo this instead.\n\n31\n00:01:40,051 --> 00:01:42,138\nTeach information skills explicitly,\n\n32\n00:01:42,158 --> 00:01:44,857\nlike evaluating sources and searching well.\n\n33\n00:01:45,303 --> 00:01:48,805\nDesign study and class time for one task at a time.\n\n34\n00:01:49,143 --> 00:01:51,138\nAnd don't assume age predicts skill,\n\n35\n00:01:51,158 --> 00:01:52,449\nin either direction.\n\n36\n00:01:52,911 --> 00:01:54,776\nOne tip to share with students: one task,\n\n37\n00:01:55,016 --> 00:01:57,701\none screen, during study.\n\n38\n00:01:57,871 --> 00:01:59,630\nNo one is born digital.\n\n39\n00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:02,083\nSkills with information are learned,\n\n40\n00:02:02,224 --> 00:02:03,331\nand they can be taught.\n\n"